#. type: Title =
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Factory Controller"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:4
msgid ""
"The factory controller is the core of this mod. Once placed in the world, "
"you may interact with the block to open its xref:dashboard.adoc[dashboard], "
"on which you can place xref:factory-gauge.adoc[factory gauges] and "
"xref:components.adoc[other components]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "A factory controller block"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:9
msgid ""
"A factory controller block stores all components placed inside. When broken, "
"the factory controller item retains its contents, and resumes functioning "
"once placed again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crafting recipe for a factory controller"
msgstr ""

#. type: #obtaining
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:17
msgid ""
"A factory controller may be crafted from 1 factory gauge, 1 redstone link, 1 "
"stock link, 2 sturdy plates, 1 precision mechanism, 2 brass casings, and 1 "
"contraption controls, arranged as above."
msgstr ""

#. type: #redstoe
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:22
msgid ""
"When a factory controller block is powered by redstone, all xref:factory-"
"gauge.adoc[factory gauges] inside are disabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Display Link"
msgstr ""

#. type: #display-link
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Display links can be attached to a factory controller block to display "
"information about this factory controller. See the in-game ponder for the "
"usage of display links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Display boards displaying information about a factory controller"
msgstr ""

#. type: #display-link
#: ../src/factory-controller.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Each line of the display represents the status of a factory gauge inside the "
"factory controller. Only factory gauges configured to xref:factory-"
"gauge.adoc#basic-production[produce] an item are included."
msgstr ""
